hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2703","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj, narrated to us al-Muharibi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn 'Abbas (RA), and on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The hands are raised in seven places.\""\n\nAnd in this narration: \""When facing the House (the Ka'bah).\""\n\nAbu Bakr (ibn Abi Shaybah) said: \""I have not made a chapter for this narration because they (the scholars) have differed regarding this chain of narration"","" and I have clarified it in my book *al-Kabir*.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
"2704","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Shu'bah, who said: I heard Abu Qaz'ah al-Bahili narrating from al-Muhajir al-Makki, who said: Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah was asked about a man who sees the House (the Ka'bah) and raises his hands. He said: \I do not think that anyone does this except the Jews. We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he did not do this.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
